templates: gi-release.yml, the author-copied release workflow (item 7)

Without this, every third-party author either hand-writes a release
workflow (and gets the attestation shape wrong, the exact failure mode
CLAUDE.md already names twice) or has nothing to copy at all. This is a
template, never uses:-referenced, because a GI's build is not one shape the
way a plugin's is (BepInEx, ReShade, UE4SS, bare Lua all build differently)
-- only the tag trigger, the zip, the attestation and the Release stay
fixed, in one job an author fills in at one marked step.

Actions are pinned by commit SHA, resolved and verified against GitHub's
own tag refs just now (git ls-remote --tags), not recalled from training
data: actions/checkout's v4 tag is lightweight (the SHA IS the commit), but
actions/attest-build-provenance's v2 is an ANNOTATED tag, so pinning its
tag-object SHA instead of the peeled commit (refs/tags/v2^{}) would have
been exactly the "resolved the tag object instead of the commit" bug
CLAUDE.md names as one of the two worst bugs found so far in this system.

Documented in spec/games/manifest.md §5.

